---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="JavaScript & TypeScript Naming Conventions Guide - useUtils Blog" 
  description="The definitive guide to naming variables, constants, classes, functions, and files in JavaScript and TypeScript environments."
  keywords="javascript naming conventions, typescript style guide, camelcase, pascalcase, screaming snake case"
>
  <Header />

  <main class="flex-grow w-full max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 flex flex-col gap-8">
    <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-[10px] md:text-[11px] font-mono text-zinc-500 select-none" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent-emerald transition-colors">home</a>
      <span class="text-zinc-700">/</span>
      <a href="/blog" class="hover:text-accent-emerald transition-colors">blog</a>
      <span class="text-zinc-700">/</span>
      <span class="text-accent-emerald font-medium">naming-conventions-javascript</span>
    </nav>

    <!-- Post Header -->
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 border-b border-border-hairline/60 pb-6">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <span class="text-[10px] font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-accent-emerald bg-accent-emerald/10 border border-accent-emerald/10 px-2 py-0.5 rounded">
          JavaScript & TS
        </span>
        <span class="text-[10px] font-mono text-zinc-500">July 22, 2026 • 6 min read</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-50 font-sans leading-tight">
        JavaScript & TypeScript Naming Conventions: The Definitive Guide
      </h1>
      <p class="text-zinc-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
        Understand standard naming patterns in the JavaScript ecosystem for variables, components, types, and constants.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Article Content -->
    <article class="prose prose-invert max-w-none text-zinc-300 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed flex flex-col gap-6 font-sans">
      <p>
        Consistency inside codebases minimizes cognitive load. When writing JavaScript or TypeScript, developers deal with variables, callbacks, component functions, object types, classes, and environment parameters. Each has a distinct convention governed by community guidelines (like Airbnb, Google, or the TypeScript style team).
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-100 mt-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="w-1 h-5 bg-accent-emerald rounded-full"></span>
        1. Variables & Functions: camelCase
      </h2>
      <p>
        In Javascript, all variables (declared using <code>let</code>, <code>const</code>, or <code>var</code>) and function names must be declared in <strong>camelCase</strong>:
      </p>
      <pre class="bg-zinc-950 border border-border-hairline p-4 rounded-lg font-mono text-xs text-zinc-400">{`const clientResponseTime = 250;
function fetchUserData(userId) {
  // ...
}`}</pre>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-100 mt-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="w-1 h-5 bg-accent-emerald rounded-full"></span>
        2. Classes, Types, & Interfaces: PascalCase
      </h2>
      <p>
        Constructors, OOP classes, and type definitions (TypeScript interfaces, type aliases, and enums) are named in <strong>PascalCase</strong>. This capitalization of the first letter easily distinguishes instantiation symbols from standard variables:
      </p>
      <pre class="bg-zinc-950 border border-border-hairline p-4 rounded-lg font-mono text-xs text-zinc-400">{`class NetworkSocketManager {
  // ...
}

interface UserProfileDetails {
  id: string;
  email: string;
}`}</pre>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-100 mt-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="w-1 h-5 bg-accent-emerald rounded-full"></span>
        3. Global Constants: CONSTANT_CASE (Screaming Snake)
      </h2>
      <p>
        Variables that are globally immutable, configuration limits, or environment flags should use uppercase letters with underscores:
      </p>
      <pre class="bg-zinc-950 border border-border-hairline p-4 rounded-lg font-mono text-xs text-zinc-400">
const DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_LIMIT = 5000;
const API_BASE_URL = "https://api.useutils.com";
      </pre>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-100 mt-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="w-1 h-5 bg-accent-emerald rounded-full"></span>
        4. UI Components: PascalCase
      </h2>
      <p>
        React, Vue, and Svelte mandate PascalCase for custom element definitions. Since standard elements like <code>&lt;div&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> are lowercased, JSX engines require uppercase names to recognize custom definitions:
      </p>
      <pre class="bg-zinc-950 border border-border-hairline p-4 rounded-lg font-mono text-xs text-zinc-400">{`export function SidebarNavigationPanel() {
  return &lt;aside&gt;&lt;nav&gt;&lt;/nav&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;;
}`}</pre>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-100 mt-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="w-1 h-5 bg-accent-emerald rounded-full"></span>
        Refactoring JS/TS Identifiers
      </h2>
      <p>
        During project migrations or variable mappings, translating schemas between database snake_case and TypeScript camelCase requires fast tools. Access our case formatters to automate this task:
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 mt-2">
        <a 
          href="/tools/pascal-case-converter"
          class="flex-grow p-4 bg-panel border border-border-hairline rounded-xl hover:border-accent-emerald/30 text-xs font-mono text-zinc-200 hover:text-accent-emerald flex items-center justify-between"
        >
          <span>PascalCase Converter</span>
          <span>→</span>
        </a>
        <a 
          href="/tools/case-converter"
          class="flex-grow p-4 bg-panel border border-border-hairline rounded-xl hover:border-accent-emerald/30 text-xs font-mono text-zinc-200 hover:text-accent-emerald flex items-center justify-between"
        >
          <span>General Case Converter</span>
          <span>→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
